    <item>
      <title>Overload Set</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/extras/overload-set/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Jul 2025 23:43:19 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/extras/overload-set/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;overload-set&#34;&gt;Overload Set&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An overload set is, essentially, a candidate set of functions that can be invoked&#xA;on a given argument. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution.html&#34;&gt;overload resolution&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Note that this simplified example doesn&amp;rsquo;t consider inherited types, and low-cost implicit conversions. Refer to the rules of &lt;a href=&#34;https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/overload_resolution.html&#34;&gt;overload resolution&lt;/a&gt; for specific rules motivating overload selection.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-cpp&#34; data-lang=&#34;cpp&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;my_specific_overload_set&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (1)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;operator&lt;/span&gt;()(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; A &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;a) { &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/* Do something with a const A*/&lt;/span&gt; }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (2)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;operator&lt;/span&gt;()(B &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;b) { &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/* Do something with a B*/&lt;/span&gt; }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (3)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;operator&lt;/span&gt;()(C c) { &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/* Do something with a copied or pure A*/&lt;/span&gt; }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (4) Sink function, accepts everything else&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;template&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;operator&lt;/span&gt;()(T &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;&amp;amp;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;other) { &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;/* Do something with a perfect-forwarded T */&lt;/span&gt; }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;};&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    A a;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    B b;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    C c;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    D d;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    my_specific_overload_set f{};&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    f(a); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (1)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    f(b); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (2)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    f(c); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (3)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    f(d); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (4)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;    f(A{}); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// (4)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;automatic-overload-set--c17&#34;&gt;Automatic overload set (≥ C++17)&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since C++17 bestowed variadic using statements on us, an automatic overload set&#xA;is very simply defined as:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>C&#43;&#43; Variant From Scratch</title>
      <link>//localhost:1313/posts/variant/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Jul 2025 23:34:30 +0200</pubDate>
      <guid>//localhost:1313/posts/variant/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;c-variant-from-scratch&#34;&gt;C++ Variant From Scratch&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE&lt;/strong&gt;: As of 26. july, this post is still incomplete. I&amp;rsquo;m sure I&amp;rsquo;ll get&#xA;around to it eventually. Don&amp;rsquo;t expect any kind of mind-blowing writing prowess to shine through just yet.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;For quite some time now, I&amp;rsquo;ve been wanting to do a full-scale implementation&#xA;of &lt;code&gt;std::variant&lt;/code&gt; from scratch. Why would you want to put yourself through&#xA;the torment, you ask? Here&amp;rsquo;s what I say:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Your understanding of the STL deepens.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Your template metaprogramming chops get their much needed exercise.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;You get your chance to make your sacrifice to the ever-benevolent standards library devs.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ol&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;By the end of this exercise you&amp;rsquo;re likely going to fall into one of two categories (insert there are 10 kinds of people joke here):&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Hello</title>
